Install Extension from .vsix File



Open VS Code  
Start Visual Studio Code.

Open Command Palette

Windows/Linux: Ctrl + Shift + P

macOS: Cmd + Shift + P

Run the Install Command  
Type:

Code
Extensions: Install from VSIX...
and select it.

Choose the File  
A file picker will open. Navigate to the location of your .vsix file, select it, and click Open.

Reload if Needed  
VS Code may ask you to reload after installation. Do that, and the extension will be ready to use.





Tip: You can also install via terminal if you have the code command available:

code --install-extension yolish-1.0.0.vsix